      "constraints": [
        "Preserve narrative prose and authored soundscape as one versioned composition; reader and Studio preview use the same document and experience model.",
        "Keep chapter identity stable and published revisions immutable; draft edits must not remove live publication. Atomic database publication remains intended and requires actual transaction proof.",
        "Enforce visibility and asset credentials on the server; expose published audio through bounded signed URLs. Local storage and mocked R2 fixtures do not prove hosted R2 or database policy.",
        "Require explicit reader audio consent, independent controls, reduced motion and accessible navigation; source fixtures do not establish rendered accessibility or browser playback.",
        "Preserve legacy manifest, chapter content and platform implementation until an explicit retirement decision; this metadata neither executes migration nor declares v2 cutover.",
        "Keep native apps, billing, multi-tenant collaboration, realtime coediting and advanced automation deferred as documented in the v2 target."
