      "handoff_review": "Narrative composition and reading are the product spine in PRODUCT.md and the v2 target. Current Next reader/Studio, shared composition readiness, transactional publication/rollback, private assets and reader identity are explicit seams. Legacy manifest/script reader and platform import-staging/editorial/audio/auth APIs remain preserved implementation lanes; no retirement inferred. Staged imports validate metadata before approval, publishing compiles snapshots, and v2 publishing locks the exact draft/chapter before updating publication plus audit in one transaction. Audio transport is an explicit reader control; browser permission/playback and reduced-motion/accessibility require direct evidence. Exact build, launcher, fixture and runtime support paths are included; their presence is not independent behavioral proof. Rollback fixture proves pure draft creation only, not atomic database publication; reader query fixtures do not verify persisted reader state or native browser behavior. The atomic publication behavior remains an explicit unbound proof gap.",
